## Database Selection Guide

### When to Use PostgreSQL

- Complex queries và advanced analytics
- JSONB data với frequent querying
- Full-text search requirements
- Geospatial data (PostGIS)
- Vector similarity search (pgvector)
- Multi-tenant applications với Row-Level Security
- Enterprise applications requiring strict ACID
- Distributed systems requiring UUID primary keys

### When to Use MySQL

- Web applications, especially LAMP/LEMP stack
- High write throughput requirements
- Simple CRUD operations
- Applications already in PHP/LAMP ecosystem
- Medium-scale applications
- When ecosystem and community support is priority

### When to Use SQL Server

- .NET applications và Windows environment
- Deep integration với Microsoft ecosystem
- Enterprise features required (SSRS, SSAS, SSIS)
- Always On Availability Groups requirement
- Temporal tables for audit trails
- In-Memory OLTP for high-throughput
- organizations already invested in Microsoft stack

### Hybrid/Multi-Database Strategy

Consider using multiple databases for different purposes:
- PostgreSQL: Primary application database, complex queries
- Redis: Caching, sessions, real-time features
- MySQL: Legacy data, read-heavy analytics
- SQL Server: Specific enterprise integrations

